    description: 'Fresh & raw, bergamot, ambroxan, Haitian vetiver. Masculine, powerful.',
    longDescription: "Dior Sauvage is the world's best-selling men's fragrance — a monumental scent that reimagined masculinity in perfumery when it launched in 2015. Created by master perfumer François Demachy exclusively using natural raw materials, Sauvage draws inspiration from wide-open spaces and the raw, arid desert under a blazing sun.\n\nThe opening is an explosive burst of Calabrian bergamot — freshly squeezed and intensely citrusy — that immediately distinguishes Sauvage from anything else in a department store. This brightness gives way to a spicy, magnetic heart of Sichuan pepper and lavender, before the legendary ambroxan base locks the scent firmly to skin. Ambroxan, a synthetic equivalent of ambergris, is the molecule responsible for Sauvage's extraordinary longevity and its distinctive animal-musky signature that gets compliments from strangers.\n\nHaitian vetiver and patchouli in the base add earthy depth and sophistication without heaviness. The 100ml Eau de Toilette is the purest, crispest expression — brighter and more outdoorsy than the Eau de Parfum. This is a safe, versatile scent appropriate for every season, occasion, and age — yet it never feels generic. An exceptional entry point for anyone building a first fragrance wardrobe.",
