    price: 195.00, originalPrice: 220.00,
    description: 'Cardamom, iris, papyrus, sandalwood, musky. Unisex, cult scent.',
    longDescription: "Le Labo Santal 33 is the most culturally significant fragrance of the 21st century — a scent so omnipresent in certain social circles it became a cultural shorthand and inspired countless think-pieces. Created for Le Labo's New York City launch in 2011, it was designed as a love letter to the American West: vast landscapes, open skies, smoky campfires, and worn leather.\n\nThe composition achieves something genuinely difficult in perfumery — it smells intensely recognisable yet impossible to categorise. Cardamom and iris provide a cool, slightly medicinal opening that immediately signals luxury. Ambrox (another ambergris-derivative) and musky violet provide the warm, deeply human skin-scent quality that makes Santal 33 feel like it's been absorbed into your skin rather than sitting on top of it. Australian sandalwood in the base is creamy and warm, perfectly integrated with papyrus and cedar.\n\nSantal 33 is genuinely unisex — it smells equally compelling on all bodies and genders. It performs exceptionally well in all seasons but particularly shines in cooler months. Extraordinarily long-lasting: spritz in the morning and you will still detect it the next day. Le Labo hand-presses the label in-store with the customer's name and date, adding a layer of personalisation unique to the brand.",
