    price: 185.00,
    description: 'Bergamot, lemon, pepper, juniper berries, sandalwood, vanilla, amber.',
    longDescription: "Byredo Gypsy Water is the fragrance that established the Swedish niche house as a global force in luxury perfumery and remains its most beloved creation. Founder Ben Gorham — the son of an Indian mother and Canadian father — created Gypsy Water to capture the romantic nomadic spirit of Romani culture: freedom, wandering, open fires in the forest, and the smell of the earth after rain.\n\nThe opening is luminous and aromatic — bergamot and lemon provide radiant citrus brightness, while black pepper and juniper berries introduce an unexpected wild, piney edge that immediately sets Gypsy Water apart from conventional perfumery. The heart is clean and ethereal with notes of incense and pine needles that evoke a forest at dawn. The base is where the fragrance becomes addictive: sandalwood, vanilla, and amber create a warm, creamy, gourmand-adjacent richness that makes Gypsy Water impossible to stop smelling.\n\nGypsy Water strikes a rare balance between fresh and warm, masculine and feminine, simple and complex. It performs beautifully in every season and on every skin type. The minimalist all-black bottle is architectural and design-forward, perfectly reflecting the Byredo aesthetic. One of the few niche fragrances that justifies its price through genuine uniqueness — nothing in mainstream perfumery smells remotely like it.",
