    longDescription: "Trek Marlin 7 is the definitive entry-level mountain bike for riders who want genuine trail capability without the compromises of budget departme-store alternatives. Built on Trek's Alpha Aluminum frame — butted tubing that removes material from areas that don't need strength and adds it where they do — the Marlin 7 achieves a stiffness-to-weight ratio that riders upgrading from cheaper bikes immediately feel.\n\nThe SR Suntour XCM 100mm travel fork absorbs roots, rocks, and technical trail features with controlled damping — a dramatic improvement over rigid forks on entry-level bikes. Shimano's 3x8 drivetrain provides 24 gears spanning a wide range from steep climbing to downhill speed. Hydraulic disc brakes on both wheels deliver consistent, modulated stopping power in wet and muddy conditions where mechanical brakes fade unpredictably.\n\nThe 29-inch wheels roll over obstacles more efficiently than 27.5-inch alternatives and maintain momentum on flat sections. Internal cable routing protects the derailleur cables from mud and brush damage on technical descents. The Marlin 7 geometry strikes a confidence-inspiring balance for beginner-to-intermediate riders: stable enough to feel secure on descents but manoeuvrable enough for technical switchbacks. Covers cross-country trails, forest paths, and weekend adventures with equal aplomb.",
