    id: 's013', slug: 'giro-synthe-mips-helmet', name: 'Giro Synthe MIPS Helmet', brand: 'Giro',
    price: 249.99, originalPrice: 299.99,
    description: 'MIPS protection, Roc Loc 5 fit system, 24 vents, aerodynamic, 210g.',
    longDescription: "Giro Synthe MIPS is the helmet that introduced aerodynamic road helmet design to the mainstream — proving that a helmet can simultaneously be the fastest, best-ventilated, and most protective option in its class. The Synthe's wind-tunnel-optimised exterior shell achieves aerodynamic drag figures comparable to traditional aero helmets while providing 24 deep-channelled vents that make it feel as cool as an open-face road helmet.\n\nMIPS (Multi-directional Impact Protection System) is the most important safety innovation in helmet design in decades. An internal low-friction layer allows the helmet to rotate slightly upon oblique impact — the most common type in real falls — redirecting energy away from the brain and reducing rotational force by up to 40% compared to traditional helmets. This technology is now standard in premium helmets across cycling, skiing, and equestrian sports.\n\nGiro's Roc Loc 5 fit system adjusts precisely to head circumference and back-of-head position with one hand, ensuring the helmet sits in the correct position without pressure hotspots. At 210 grams, the Synthe is among the lightest premium road helmets available. Integrated lens channels accommodate Giro eyewear for a seamlessly unified system. The Synthe is used by professional cyclists in the Tour de France and World Tour races — a real-world test environment of aerodynamic performance, structural integrity, and comfort under extreme conditions.",
